title: Write the pidly shell script
desc:14
A single POSIX shell script providing the ergonomics layer over the format.
Not a runtime dependency: every command must be something a person could
have done by hand with mkdir, mv, and an editor, leaving the repository
byte-identical.

The one exception is claiming, which needs the lock in 8 to be safe under
concurrent agents. Everything else stays hand-doable.

Subcommands are broken out as child tickets. 13 is the entry point for a
project that has no tracker yet.
